From: RTSP-on-GE contributors
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Map the already-advertised H.264 elementary-stream subtype

MFVideoFormat_H264_ES is already registered and accepted, but it is a
non-FourCC GUID and currently resolves to AV_CODEC_ID_NONE. Match the
complete GUID to the existing H264 decoder, preserving other GUID tails
and the existing FourCC paths. Existing no-extradata H264 parsing remains
unchanged; this adds no fragment assembler or codec-data conversion.

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -170,6 +170,8 @@
     DWORD fourcc = mfvf->guidFormat.Data1;
     enum AVCodecID id = av_codec_get_id( tables, fourcc );
 
+    /* This already-advertised MF subtype is a full GUID, not a FourCC. */
+    if (IsEqualGUID( &mfvf->guidFormat, &MFVideoFormat_H264_ES )) return AV_CODEC_ID_H264;
     if (id != AV_CODEC_ID_NONE) return id;
 
     switch (fourcc)
